0235">https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 16:30:08 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sam Altman on the role of government in AI]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1904933748015255552/k43GMz63_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Sam Altman (@sama) on X</p><p>I would like to clarify a few things. First, the obvious one: we do not have or want government guarantees for OpenAI datacenters. We believe that governments should not pick winners or losers, and that taxpayers should not bail out companies that make bad business decisions or</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007">https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 16:30:08 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Further discussion of Kosmos, the “AI scientist.”]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G5F4dabaYAAO51a.png:large"></p><p>Niko McCarty. (@NikoMcCarty) on X</p><p>I finally read the Kosmos “AI Scientist” paper from FutureHouse. Here is a bit about what they did and what I think about it. &gt; The general idea behind this paper, and others like it, is that science follows a series of steps and that much of these steps can be automated. Those</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/NikoMcCarty/status/1986501362730082464">https://x.com/NikoMcCarty/status/1986501362730082464</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/NikoMcCarty/status/1986501362730082464</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/NikoMcCarty/status/1986501362730082464</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 16:30:08 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tony Kulesa (@kulesatony) on X]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1380556438209241090/Eky5Ip0a_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Tony Kulesa (@kulesatony) on X</p><p>I finished my PhD with more questions than answers. I had built huge screening datasets, there was just too much data to explore. The first thing I did when I got access to Kosmos was throw in some of these datasets. Honestly, my jaw dropped at the result. Try it yourself:</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/kulesatony/status/1986089961670709441">https://x.com/kulesatony/status/1986089961670709441</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/kulesatony/status/1986089961670709441</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/kulesatony/status/1986089961670709441</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 16:30:08 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Those new service sector jobs]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/01/german-museum-grumpy-guide-kunstpalast-dusseldorf">https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/01/german-museum-grumpy-guide-kunstpalast-dusseldorf</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.co